  "notes": "A Descript-like audio story editor scaled down for high-school language students. Warm off-white paper background (#f4f2ed) with a teal primary; each clip type has its own color (teal narration, ochre sounds, indigo/pink interviews) carried consistently through the bin color bars, transcript speaker names, waveform bars and timeline clips. Teacher feedback is numbered amber dots that appear in three places at once: ruler, waveform overview and inline in the transcript, plus cards in the right panel with 'still in your story' yellow callouts that check the student's current edit against the comment. Length meter shows a 4:00 target line in red dashed on the ruler, over-time area hatched pink. Keyboard keycaps legend (Space play, S split, Del cut, ⌘Z undo) in the tab bar. Story order tab (verified live) is a numbered list with drag handles and up/down arrows; Rubric tab shows a 75/100 score with criterion bars. Timeline has a 'magnetic' main Story track and a secondary 'Under the voice' bed track."
